      "html": "<figure id=\"S2.T1\" class=\"ltx_table\">\n<figcaption class=\"ltx_caption\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_table\">Table 1: </span>The real AME<math id=\"S2.T1.m8\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"(4,6)\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(4,6)</annotation></semantics></math> state of Eq. (<a href=\"#S2.E1\" title=\"In II A real AME(4,6) state ‣ Euler’s thirty-six officers need not all be entangled:real AME(4,6), families and classification\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag\">1</span></a>) as Euler’s array of officers: row <math id=\"S2.T1.m9\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"a\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a</annotation></semantics></math> (rank), column <math id=\"S2.T1.m10\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"b\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b</annotation></semantics></math>\n(regiment), entry <math id=\"S2.T1.m11\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\ket{\\phi_{ab}}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mo fence=\"false\" rspace=\"0.167em\">|</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ket{\\phi_{ab}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the unnormalized state of the third and fourth party. Shaded: the <math id=\"S2.T1.m12\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"12\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mn>12</mn><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">12</annotation></semantics></math> classical\nofficers <math id=\"S2.T1.m13\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\sqrt{2}\\,\\ket{cd}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo lspace=\"0.170em\" rspace=\"0em\">​<